From 9ccc0b022d8ae148d3ce1fa415f99a3cf15ab004 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Knifethrower <132020881+Knifethrower@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 13:43:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ruffle_sdl: the software cursor follows the movie
 (Mouse.hide, hand over buttons)

The software cursor of 0100 showed after every mouse motion, also in games
that call Mouse.hide() and draw their own pointer, which then showed two.
The Flash Player's cursor follows the movie, and so does this one now:

* Mouse.hide() hides it, Mouse.show() brings it back (the player tells the
  UI backend; ruffle_sdl now has one that records this instead of the
  NullUiBackend)
* over buttons and links (MouseCursor::Hand and Grab) the built in arrow
  turns into a pointing hand of the same height, box filtered like the
  arrow. A custom RUFFLE_SW_CURSOR_IMAGE stays as it is.

RUFFLE_SW_CURSOR_FOLLOW_MOVIE=0 turns this off (the cursor of 0100 as it
was).

tests/cursor_test.sh (x86_64, Xvfb): the new cases movie_hide,
movie_hide_ignored and button_hand pass, and so do the original runnable
cases, the off case still pixel identical to a build without 0100.
Machinarium on the same PC and on an RG Cube XX (Knulli, KMSDRM, Mali-G31,
with 0100 and 0101 on the series): the arrow, and the hand over hotspots and
buttons.

